  "body": "stacked on #1634 - review only after 881f7726; merge #1615, #1622, #1634 first. (fork synced at v0.18.0)\n\n## What was found (reproduced before any fix)\n\n#1635 asked whether a stock-source cross drill that enters a part posts unjudged. It does not. `cross_part::part_clear` read the source's mesh, and off the stock that mesh is the stock itself. So EVERY stock-source cross drill was refused at generation, the illegal ones and the legal ones alike, with \"cross hole ... rapids into the finished part\". The stock was read as the solid to keep. Nothing reached the post, so this is not a P1. It is a false refusal of legal programs, which is P3 by the AGENTS.md table (left at P1 for the maintainer to lower).\n\nReadings: #117 punched bar r10 with one r2 hole plunging -X from (10, 0, 0), 6 mm deep. Stocks: an r20 bar and a 40 x 40 box, each aligned and turned a quarter about Z. Mill-turn and lathe benches. Stock-source op S1.\n\n| case | before (all four stocks) | now |\n|---|---|---|\n| hole where the bar models none | refused: \"rapids into the finished part\" (meaning the stock) | refused: \"cuts into the finished part: the drill meets steel at the mouth - the model has no hole there\" |\n| into the bar's modelled hole | refused, same words | generates the part source's chain, move for move; posts |\n| stock-only material (r3 core) | refused, same words | generates; posts |\n| lathe, box stock, legal hole | refused: \"cannot be read as turned\" (that is the box) | generates |\n\n## What changed\n\n- `cross_spindle::cross_drill` takes `Solids { source, stock, kept }`.\n  - On a part source: unchanged (the part, the setup's stock, the part).\n  - On a stock source: the setup's parts are the solid it measures and keeps, and the source stock is the raw material its mouths stand off. This is exactly the chain a part-source cross drill drills in that stock.\n- `keep_law::is_cross_drill` joins `is_stock_kept_kind`, so `parts_in_stock` returns the setup's parts for it. Fixtures and a stock-only model are left out.\n- The 2D tail's vertical solid law against those parts skips a cross drill (`parts_crossed`). The radial law has already judged the chain, and the solid law with no wall excuse would convict a drill sized to a faceted cross hole.\n- On a plain lathe, a stock-source cross drill reads the parts as the turned work, not the box stock.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/1635-stock-cross-drill.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nPins in `crates/app/tests/stock_source_cross_drill.rs` (new):\n- `a_stock_source_cross_drill_into_the_part_is_refused_by_name_on_both_stocks`\n- `a_stock_source_cross_drill_into_the_parts_own_hole_or_stock_only_material_posts` (also asserts the chain equals the part source's)\n- `a_stock_source_cross_drill_at_the_modelled_holes_size_is_excused_its_faceted_wall`\n- `a_stock_source_cross_drill_with_no_part_in_the_setup_keeps_nothing`\n- `a_lathe_reads_the_turned_part_in_a_box_stock_not_the_box`\n- `over_mcp_a_stock_source_cross_drill_answers_for_the_part_the_same` (built-in Mill-turn, MCP's default Stock source)\n\nSix mutations, each checked red and then reverted. The table is in the decision file.\n\nQuick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green on da340c0f: sim 102 s, motion 6 s, app 1262 s, ui 59 s, 0 failed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The 3+2 frame arm's `parts_crossed` guard. A cross drill is lathe or mill-turn work and does not reach that arm.\n- A posted program on a plain lathe. The bench mounts no turning post.\n- MCP on a turned stock. MCP's `set_stock` takes no rotation.\n\n## Follow-up\n\nA part-source cross drill still answers only to its own source, not to #1621's neighbouring parts.\n\nChangelog: A cross drill taken off the stock is judged against the parts the stock holds, not against the stock: drilling a part's own cross hole off the raw bar now generates and posts, and a hole into a part where it models none is refused by name (#1635).\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1635\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
